# v42 — scale_act even-row stride hypothesis

## Differential audit finding
Original MixLLM activation quantization stores scales as [K/128, M_even], padding the row dimension to an even count. The current SM75 quantizer allocates [K/128, M]. The current kernel also assumes scale_act stride exactly rows and indexes scale_act[group * rows + r]. This is a concrete memory-layout mismatch, not a guessed tuning change.

## Single hypothesis
Padding scale_act rows to M_even and using the actual padded row stride in the SM75 kernel may improve half-load alignment/coalescing on T4 while preserving the same activation values for all real rows.

## Controlled change
Only activation-scale allocation/stride handling will change. input_int8 values, quantization formula, weight packing, model, benchmark settings, and precision assignments remain unchanged. The kernel will reject undersized scale tensors but accept padded scale_act with size(1) >= rows and use scale_act.size(1) as the row stride.

## Falsification criteria
Any correctness failure, changed outputs beyond the existing tolerance, or no performance improvement will reject the hypothesis and trigger restoration/next audit.
